    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on a high-ceiling matchup against Gibson today, positioning **Kyle Tucker** (77.19) and **Andy Pages** (72.65) as our primary offensive anchors. Both benefit significantly from a favorable SP_xERA of 5.63, and while their lineup spots remain pending, their base projections combined with high-leverage scoring spots make them must-starts. The day's standout efficiency, however, belongs to **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29). Facing Roki Sasaki, **Gunnar Henderson** gains a massive boost from the matchup\u2019s stolen base potential; Sasaki\u2019s notoriously slow delivery allows us to weaponize **Gunnar Henderson**\u2019s speed against an elite arm, effectively mitigating the threat posed by Sasaki\u2019s talent and making him our premier play of the day.\n\nWe are leaning heavily into platoon and park advantages elsewhere, as seen with **Nolan Schanuel** (67.22) and **Josh Jung** (65.52). **Nolan Schanuel** enjoys a +10% park boost, while **Josh Jung** leverages a +19% skill advantage against a favorable matchup. The most difficult decision on the bench was **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (54.36), who was narrowly squeezed out by a surplus of higher-scoring infielders. Despite a strong +14% platoon edge, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** fell short of the daily efficiency threshold required to displace **Brayan Rocchio** or **Jacob Wilson**, as the optimizer favored the latter's volume in the order and specific park-driven upside.\n\nWe must remain cautious with **Jackson Merrill** (52.34), who faces the elite deGrom. While **Jackson Merrill** maintains a strong projected score, he is facing a pitcher who effectively neutralizes stolen base opportunities, reducing his impact in our scarcity-focused build. Additionally, **Wade Meckler** (45.60) remains a fringe play; despite the favorable park, his L/L platoon disadvantage and low spot in the batting order make him a high-risk start. We will monitor the lineups for **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages** closely, as any shift down the order would necessitate a recalibration of our expected runs and RBI output.",
